<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11996" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπευθής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυνθάνομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not inquired into, unknown,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κείνου δ᾽ . . ὄλεθρον ἀπευθέα θῆκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.88
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				259
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀκοῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.
				</span></i>
			 Tyr. <i><span class="en">
				17.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not inquiring, ignorant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦλθον . . ἀπευθής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.184
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cerc.
				5.3
			</span></i>: c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				194
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.303
			</span></i>.</div>
